# effect_transitive_user_op — effect coverage flows up through a called user op
# (README §15/§17 #5, WS2-040). `announce` performs `write console.stdout`; `main`
# activates it, so the write effect flows UP into main's effective set and must be
# covered there — `main` declares `effect write console.stdout` and `uses` the
# granting capability. Drop main's `uses` and the gate rejects it (uncovered
# transitive effect).
#
# Correctness observation: main's effective effects include announce's write.
# Expected output: the announced line + PASS + `---- 2 passed, 0 failed ----`

EffectTransitiveUserOp is project
EffectTransitiveUserOp module examplesEffectTransitiveUserOp
EffectTransitiveUserOp target console
EffectTransitiveUserOp entry main

examplesEffectTransitiveUserOp is module
examplesEffectTransitiveUserOp path examples.effectTransitiveUserOp
examplesEffectTransitiveUserOp exports main
examplesEffectTransitiveUserOp purpose "Cover an effect that flows up from a called op"
examplesEffectTransitiveUserOp invariant "main covers announce's transitive write effect"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout

announce is operation
announce in line String
announce out Int64
announce effect write console.stdout
announce uses stdoutWriter
announce memory heap no
announce async no
announce purpose "Write a line (an effect that flows up to the caller)"
announce invariant "Performs one console write; returns 0"
announce let zero immutable Int64 0
announce do emit
announce return zero
emit is call
emit in announce
emit invokes console.writeLine
emit arg text String line

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memory heap no
main async no
main purpose "Activate announce and assert the harness passes"
main invariant "Covers announce's transitive effect; writes the summary"
main let banner immutable String "transitive effect covered"
main let harnessName immutable String "effect_transitive_user_op"
main let harnessExpected immutable Int64 0
main let nonZeroDecoy immutable Int64 1
main let noopName immutable String "effect_transitive_user_op: announce returned its real 0"
main do callAnnounce
main do writeResult
main do noopCheck
main do harnessReport
main return harnessSummaryCode

callAnnounce is call
callAnnounce in main
callAnnounce invokes announce
callAnnounce arg line String banner
callAnnounce out announceCode Int64

writeResult is call
writeResult in main
writeResult invokes test.assertEqualInt64
writeResult arg name String harnessName
writeResult arg expected Int64 harnessExpected
writeResult arg actual Int64 announceCode

noopCheck is call
noopCheck in main
noopCheck invokes test.assertNotEqualInt64
noopCheck arg name String noopName
noopCheck arg expected Int64 nonZeroDecoy
noopCheck arg actual Int64 announceCode

harnessReport is call
harnessReport in main
harnessReport invokes test.summary
harnessReport out harnessSummaryCode ExitCode
